WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Egypt connects northeast Africa with the Middle East along the life-giving Nile River valley.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Mount Catherine on the Sinai Peninsula reaches 2,629 meters as Egypt's highest mountain summit.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
The Great Pyramid of Giza was built around 2560 BC, standing 146 meters tall as an ancient wonder.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Traditional attire features the breezy cotton Galabeya robe woven from premium Egyptian cotton.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Traditional Egyptian cuisine features Koshari lentils and pasta with spicy tomato vinegar sauce.

